Logical partition of code
    A package is a namespace that organizes a set of related classes and interfaces.
    similar to folder in our computers.
    Adds permissions.

For example - java.util is a package its components (interfaces implementations etc...) all logically belong to the same package
and they are closely related.

Class members access permissions when we import a package and we try to access a default member of the class that is contained
within the imported package we will get a compilation error since default doesn't grant access to those outside the package.
classes can be defined as default as well thus they won't be accessible from outside the package.
the public classes define the package API.